have you ever wondered how terraform  detects if a given resource creation  depends on another resource watch this  short to find out the answer  terraform can handle two types of  dependencies implicit and explicit  implicit dependencies are known to  terraform and are detected automatically  for example a compute instance must be  created after VPC because this is  implicit of terraform the order you  write your infrastructure code is not  important  explicit dependencies are unknown to  terraform and must be configured  explicitly using the depends on argument  for example let's say You must create  two VMS a server and a client and you  want the client VM only to be created  after the server VM is successfully  created this dependency is not visible  to terraform and has to be explicitly  mentioned are you ready to learn more  click on the three dots and then click  on the link in the description box to  enroll in the getting started with  terraform for Google Cloud course see  you there
 

